Are you welcoming, organised and do you enjoy making sure everything in the office runs smoothly? For our client in Amsterdam, we are looking for an office coordinator who enjoys taking a hands-on approach and combining a variety of responsibilities. As an office coordinator, you and your colleagues ensure a welcoming and well-organised working environment. You combine reception and general office duties with administrative and logistics support. You are the main point of contact at the office and independently make sure everything runs smoothly. Your responsibilities include:  - Welcoming employees, visitors and external partners;
 - Providing reception and front desk support;
 - Carrying out administrative tasks;
 - Coordinating lunch, deliveries and suppliers;
 - Coordinating repair and maintenance requests;
 - Processing orders and preparing shipping documents and labels;
 - Supporting the Office Manager with day-to-day activities.


Wij bieden
  - A gross hourly wage of € 17,23;
 - A part-time position for 20-24 hours per week;
 - Flexible working hours and days;
 - A varied position within an international working environment;
 - Plenty of independence and responsibility;
 - An enthusiastic and committed team in Amsterdam.



 - Has an MBO/HBO level of education and thinking;
 - Is welcoming, friendly and service-oriented;
 - Works in an organised and accurate manner;
 - Has a good command of English and preferably communicates well in Dutch;
 - Is available around lunchtime from Monday to Thursday and for the full day on Friday;
 - Is flexible and occasionally available for additional hours during holidays or sick leave.

Are you a solid Production Worker with an eye for detail? Then this Garden Furniture Production job is your new job!
Acerca de la empresaFor over seventy years, Keter has been inspiring people around the world with great, innovative high-end products for in home and gardens. The products are sold in 100 different countries, multiple design awards and product of the year awards are won by this company. To keep this quality high they are looking for a Production employee.
 Working hours as a Production Worker 3 shifts are: 6:50-15:00, 14:50-23:00 en 22:50-7:00.
Sobre el trabajoIn this full-time job, you will be reponsible for all production work around the injection molding machine. You will pack products and prepare them for departure. You will also keep an eye on the inventory of the machines. Thanks to you, the production process runs smoothly!
  - You understand and speak/write English;
 - You have a hands-on mentality;
 - You are reliable;
 - You find it no problem to perform multiple tasks.

Requisitos - Some experience in a factory environment is a plus;
 - Preferably English or Dutch speaking;
 - Flexibility for shift work.
 - EU nationality.

Qué ofrecemos - €14,99 + 20% shift bonus becomes €17,99;
 - Full-time job;
 - Flexible working hours;
 - Good working conditions;
 - Travel allowances.

BOOST YOUR CAREER & BALANCE YOUR LIFE IN THE NETHERLANDS 


WE ARE LOOKING FOR DOCTORS! 
Our clients are mental health institutions and occupational health companies, seeking Doctors for various locations across the country. 

MENTAL HEALTH & OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH 
We support you with: 
•    language course 
•    Accommodation 
•    integration in the country 
•    and much more... 


Doctors to work in Mental Health Institutions 
•    Starting monthly salary: €4977 (after specialization, monthly salary up to €10.616); 
•    With or without experience or specialization; 
•    Several locations around the country; 
•    Coverage of home-to-work travel costs; 36-hour workweek; 
•    Offer of Dutch language training A1-B2+ (online + in-person) + books + scholarship during the online training for personal expenses + accommodation and food allowance during the in-person training. 

 OCCUPATIONAL HEALTH  

Doctors to work in Occupational Health 
•    Starting monthly salary; €4000-€5.066 + annual progression; 
•    With or without experience or specialization. 
•    Several locations around the country 
•    Coverage of home-to-work travel costs; 40-hour workweek; 
•    Offer of Dutch language training A1-B2+ (online + in-person) + books + scholarship during the online training for personal expenses + accommodation and food allowance during the in-person training. 



Other benefits all our vacancies have in common: 
•    Annual salary progression; 
•    Year-end bonus (8.33% of your annual salary); Holiday allowance (8.33% of your annual salary); Support with finding a fully furnished home ready for immediate move-in; 
•    Support/assistance in work and private life, through a coach; 
•    Big register costs; 
•    Dutch official language exam costs. 

Additional benefits may also be available depending on the employer. 


CORE REQUIREMENTS     
•    Good English level; Degree in the EU; 
•    Time and dedication to attend the Dutch course. 

Please note that additional requirements may apply depending on the specific vacancy. 


LANGUAGE TRAINING     
Our Dutch Language Training (A1-B2+) begins with 11 weeks of online classes, followed by 6 weeks of in-person classes in Portugal, and then 8 weeks of in-person classes in the Netherlands. 
We cover accommodation, provide books, and offer an allowance for personal expenses. 
Once in the Netherlands, but before starting your job, enjoy additional workshops to further enhance your language skills. 

WHY THE NETHERLANDS? 
This country offers more than just a job. It provides a lifestyle! Here’s why moving could be the best decision of your life: 
•    top-tier healthcare system; 
•    work-life balance; 
•    career growth opportunities; 
•    welcoming community; 
•    cultural richness. 
If you would like to learn more about these vacancies or to be updated about other opportunities we have available, please feel free to contact us with any questions. 

